invariant: INV-14
file: cpu.h
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_host
reason: cpu_bits_ok stops requiring CH_CPU_PROBED, so a configuration
  that never set ch_cfg.cpu, 0, runs as though its caller had looked and
  found nothing. The ruling is that every caller writes the field on
  purpose (docs/decisions.md 89). The edit keeps the undefined bits
  refused, so it moves the probe's rule alone; test/tcp_blocking_loop_cpu.h
  requires ch_connect to refuse 0 before a byte leaves.

--- old
    return (cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_PROBED) != 0 && (cfg->cpu & ~(uint32_t)CH_CPU_DEFINED) == 0;
--- new
    return (cfg->cpu & ~(uint32_t)CH_CPU_DEFINED) == 0;
